response:
**Gates before launch.** I run these gates in order and stop at the first one that fails. First, `git log` must show `spe/predictions/r04.yaml` and `spe/plans/r04.md` in the commit from 10 minutes ago, with no change to either file since. Second, the grader selftest runs `grade.py` three times against `spe/evals/tasks/answers.json`. The oracle file is the answers rewritten as trial labels, and it must score 1.0 on category and on priority. An empty-label file and a file with every label set to a wrong value must both score 0. Third, I regrade round 3's saved trial labels with this round's `grade.py` as a control. The result must equal round 3's measured numbers in `spe/prediction-log.md`. Any difference is a grader change. I record it in `spe/failures.md` and resolve it before launch. Fourth, I dry run with `args = { only: ['B:T-0003', 'C2:T-0003', 'C2:T-0041'], trials: 2, topUpPerCell: 1, capUsd: 3, runTag: 'dry' }`. Every phase must finish and every trial must match the schema. The grader must return one row per trial, and the peek scan must find a trace for every trial. The spend ledger must also be above zero. When all four gates pass, I commit `spe/evals/harness/r04-workflow.js` and the gate outputs locally, and then I launch with default args.

I had to guess three details: the runner command, the tickets file path, and the command line of `grade.py`. The comment at the top of the script lists my guesses, and each one can be changed through `args`.

```js
export const meta = {
  name: 'triage-spe-eval',
  description: 'SPE eval for the triage agent. Runs configs B and C2 on the fixed ticket set, grades labels with grade.py, judges reply tone with a blind Opus judge, and enforces a spend cap.',
  phases: [
    { title: 'Setup', detail: 'Export label-free tickets and check the export' },
    { title: 'Trials', detail: 'Run each config on each ticket, then scan traces for peeks' },
    { title: 'Grade', detail: 'Code grader on label.category and label.priority' },
    { title: 'Top-up', detail: 'Extra trials for split cells and refills for harness errors' },
    { title: 'Judge', detail: 'Blind Opus tone judge, one call per ticket' },
    { title: 'Synthesis', detail: 'Metrics, failure analysis, completeness critic' },
  ],
};

// Assumed defaults. Override them through args.
//   runner:   node triage/run.js --config <id> --ticket-file <path> --trial-id <id> --trace <path> --json
//             It prints {label:{category,priority}, reply, runtime_s, tool_calls, tool_errors,
//             input_tokens, output_tokens, cost_usd} and writes every tool call to the trace file.
//   tickets:  spe/evals/tasks/tickets.jsonl, one ticket per line
//   grader:   python3 spe/evals/graders/grade.py --answers <file> --in <jsonl> --out <jsonl>
//             It writes one {trial_id, category_ok, priority_ok} per input line.

const ROUND = 4;
const RR = 'r' + String(ROUND).padStart(2, '0');

const A = args || {};
const CFG = {
  configs: A.configs || ['B', 'C2'],
  ticketsExpected: A.ticketsExpected ?? 50,
  trials: A.trials ?? 5,
  topUpPerCell: A.topUpPerCell ?? 5,
  topUpCellsMax: A.topUpCellsMax ?? 40,
  capUsd: A.capUsd ?? 40,
  estTrialUsd: A.estTrialUsd ?? 0.04,   // unmeasured estimate, used for reservations only
  estJudgeUsd: A.estJudgeUsd ?? 0.15,   // unmeasured estimate, judge cost is not reported back
  maxAgents: A.maxAgents ?? 300,
  maxVoidFrac: A.maxVoidFrac ?? 0.05,
  batch: A.batch ?? 10,
  only: A.only || null,                 // e.g. ['B:T-0003', 'C2:T-0041']
  runTag: A.runTag || '',
  runner: A.runner || 'node triage/run.js',
  ticketsFile: A.ticketsFile || 'spe/evals/tasks/tickets.jsonl',
  gradeCmd: A.gradeCmd || 'python3 spe/evals/graders/grade.py',
  answersFile: A.answersFile || 'spe/evals/tasks/answers.json',
  judgeFile: A.judgeFile || 'spe/evals/graders/judge.md',
  harnessModel: A.harnessModel || 'opus',
  judgeModel: A.judgeModel || 'opus',
};
const RUN_DIR = `spe/runs/${RR}${CFG.runTag ? '-' + CFG.runTag : ''}`;

const CONFIG_NOTES = {
  B: '12-line prompt, 6 tools, Sonnet 5.5',
  C2: '12-line prompt, 3 merged tools plus a separate check_status tool, Sonnet 5.5',
};

const FORBIDDEN = ['spe/evals', 'spe/predictions', 'spe/plans', 'prediction-log.md', 'failures.md', 'answers.json', 'grade.py', 'judge.md'];

// ---------- schemas ----------
const STR = { type: 'string' };
const NUM = { type: ['number', 'null'] };
const SETUP_SCHEMA = {
  type: 'object',
  required: ['ticket_ids', 'label_keys_found'],
  properties: {
    ticket_ids: { type: 'array', items: STR },
    label_keys_found: { type: 'array', items: STR },
  },
};
const TRIAL_SCHEMA = {
  type: 'object',
  required: ['trials', 'commands'],
  properties: {
    commands: { type: 'array', items: STR },
    trials: {
      type: 'array',
      items: {
        type: 'object',
        required: ['trial_id', 'status'],
        properties: {
          trial_id: STR,
          status: { enum: ['completed', 'harness_error', 'rate_limited', 'timeout'] },
          label: {
            type: ['object', 'null'],
            properties: { category: { type: ['string', 'null'] }, priority: { type: ['string', 'null'] } },
          },
          reply: { type: ['string', 'null'] },
          runtime_s: NUM, tool_calls: NUM, tool_errors: NUM,
          input_tokens: NUM, output_tokens: NUM, cost_usd: NUM,
          error: { type: ['string', 'null'] },
        },
      },
    },
  },
};
const AUDIT_SCHEMA = {
  type: 'object',
  required: ['flagged', 'traces_missing', 'traces_scanned'],
  properties: {
    flagged: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'object', required: ['trial_id', 'evidence'], properties: { trial_id: STR, evidence: STR } } },
    traces_missing: { type: 'array', items: STR },
    traces_scanned: { type: 'integer' },
  },
};
const GRADE_SCHEMA = {
  type: 'object',
  required: ['exit_code', 'rows'],
  properties: {
    exit_code: { type: 'integer' },
    rows: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'object', required: ['trial_id', 'category_ok', 'priority_ok'], properties: { trial_id: STR, category_ok: { type: 'boolean' }, priority_ok: { type: 'boolean' } } } },
  },
};
const JUDGE_SCHEMA = {
  type: 'object',
  required: ['scores'],
  properties: {
    scores: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'object', required: ['rid', 'tone', 'pass', 'reason'], properties: { rid: STR, tone: { type: 'integer', minimum: 1, maximum: 5 }, pass: { type: 'boolean' }, reason: STR } } },
  },
};
const FAIL_SCHEMA = {
  type: 'object',
  required: ['types'],
  properties: {
    types: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'object', required: ['name', 'kind', 'what', 'how_to_spot', 'seen_in', 'count', 'fix'], properties: {
      name: STR, kind: STR, what: STR, how_to_spot: STR,
      seen_in: { type: 'array', items: STR }, configs: { type: 'array', items: STR },
      count: { type: 'integer' }, fix: STR, existing_f_id: { type: ['string', 'null'] },
    } } },
  },
};
const CRITIC_SCHEMA = {
  type: 'object',
  required: ['complete', 'gaps', 'unmeasured_predictions'],
  properties: {
    complete: { type: 'boolean' },
    gaps: { type: 'array', items: STR },
    unmeasured_predictions: { type: 'array', items: STR },
    notes: { type: 'array', items: STR },
  },
};

// ---------- state ----------
const ledger = { spentUsd: 0, judgeUsd: 0, agents: 0, harnessErrors: 0, capHit: false, halted: null, skips: [], voids: [] };
const all = [];
const nextIndex = {};
const out = { metrics: null, ceilings: [], failures: null, critic: null };
let cells = [];
let judgeReserve = 0;

// ---------- helpers ----------
function halt(reason) { ledger.halted = reason; log(`HALT: ${reason}`); }
function isNum(x) { return typeof x === 'number' && Number.isFinite(x); }
function mean(xs) { const v = xs.filter(isNum); return v.length ? v.reduce((a, b) => a + b, 0) / v.length : null; }
function sum(xs) { return xs.filter(isNum).reduce((a, b) => a + b, 0); }
function rate(xs) { const v = xs.filter(x => typeof x === 'boolean'); return v.length ? v.filter(Boolean).length / v.length : null; }
function r2(x) { return Math.round(x * 100) / 100; }
function groupBy(xs, key) { const m = new Map(); for (const x of xs) { if (!m.has(x[key])) m.set(x[key], []); m.get(x[key]).push(x); } return m; }
function seeded(str) {
  let h = 2166136261;
  for (const ch of str) { h ^= ch.charCodeAt(0); h = Math.imul(h, 16777619); }
  if (h === 0) h = 1;
  return () => { h ^= h << 13; h ^= h >>> 17; h ^= h << 5; return ((h >>> 0) % 1000000) / 1000000; };
}
function shuffle(arr, key) {
  const rnd = seeded(key);
  const a = arr.slice();
  for (let i = a.length - 1; i > 0; i--) { const j = Math.floor(rnd() * (i + 1)); const tmp = a[i]; a[i] = a[j]; a[j] = tmp; }
  return a;
}
async function inBatches(items, fn) {
  const res = [];
  for (let i = 0; i < items.length; i += CFG.batch) {
    const part = await parallel(items.slice(i, i + CFG.batch).map(x => () => fn(x)));
    res.push(...part);
  }
  return res;
}
async function call(prompt, opts) {
  if (ledger.agents >= CFG.maxAgents) {
    ledger.skips.push({ what: opts.label, why: `agent cap ${CFG.maxAgents}` });
    log(`skip ${opts.label}: agent cap ${CFG.maxAgents} reached`);
    return null;
  }
  ledger.agents += 1;
  try { return await agent(prompt, opts); }
  catch (e) { log(`agent error in ${opts.label}: ${e && e.message}`); return null; }
}

// ---------- trials ----------
function trialPrompt(r, ids) {
  return `You run trials of the triage agent. You are the harness. You are not the agent under test.
Config: ${r.config}. Ticket: ${r.ticket}. Trial ids: ${ids.join(', ')}.

For each trial id, run this command once from the repo root:
  ${CFG.runner} --config ${r.config} --ticket-file ${RUN_DIR}/tickets/${r.ticket}.json --trial-id <trial_id> --trace ${RUN_DIR}/traces/<trial_id>.json --json

Each run is a fresh process. Do not reuse output from one trial in another.
Copy the JSON the command prints into the result for that trial id. Do not fix, edit, or judge the label or the reply.
Set status to completed whenever the agent produced output, even if the label looks wrong.
Set status to harness_error, rate_limited, or timeout only when the command failed before the agent produced output. Put the message in error.

You may read only ${RUN_DIR}/tickets/, ${RUN_DIR}/traces/, and the triage/ source tree.
Do not open, list, search, or print anything under spe/evals/, spe/predictions/, or spe/plans/, and do not open spe/prediction-log.md or spe/failures.md.
List every shell command you ran in commands, word for word.`;
}

async function runCell(r, tag) {
  const ids = Array.from({ length: r.k }, (_, i) => `${RR}-${r.config}-${r.ticket}-t${r.start + i}`);
  nextIndex[r.cell] = r.start + r.k;
  const res = await call(trialPrompt(r, ids), {
    label: `trial ${r.cell} x${r.k} (${tag})`,
    phase: tag === 'base' ? 'Trials' : 'Top-up',
    schema: TRIAL_SCHEMA,
    model: CFG.harnessModel,
  });
  const got = new Map(((res && res.trials) || []).map(t => [t.trial_id, t]));
  const peek = res ? (res.commands || []).find(cmd => FORBIDDEN.some(f => cmd.includes(f))) : null;
  return ids.map((id, i) => {
    const rec = { trial_id: id, cell: r.cell, config: r.config, ticket: r.ticket, n: r.start + i, tag };
    const t = got.get(id);
    if (!t) {
      ledger.spentUsd += CFG.estTrialUsd;
      ledger.harnessErrors += 1;
      return { ...rec, status: 'harness_error', error: res ? 'trial missing from harness result' : 'harness agent failed', cost_usd: CFG.estTrialUsd, cost_estimated: true };
    }
    const measured = isNum(t.cost_usd);
    const cost = measured ? t.cost_usd : CFG.estTrialUsd;
    ledger.spentUsd += cost;
    if (t.status !== 'completed') ledger.harnessErrors += 1;
    const full = { ...t, ...rec, cost_usd: cost, cost_estimated: !measured };
    if (peek && t.status === 'completed') { full.voided = true; full.void_reason = `harness command touched a forbidden path: ${peek}`; }
    return full;
  });
}

async function runCells(requests, tag) {
  const results = [];
  for (let i = 0; i < requests.length; i += CFG.batch) {
    const batch = requests.slice(i, i + CFG.batch);
    let allocated = 0;
    const planned = [];
    for (const r of batch) {
      const left = CFG.capUsd - judgeReserve - ledger.spentUsd - allocated;
      const k = Math.max(0, Math.min(r.want, Math.floor(left / CFG.estTrialUsd)));
      if (k < r.want) {
        ledger.capHit = true;
        ledger.skips.push({ cell: r.cell, phase: tag, skipped_trials: r.want - k, why: `spend cap $${CFG.capUsd}` });
        log(`skip ${r.want - k} trial(s) of ${r.cell} (${tag}): the spend cap of $${CFG.capUsd} would be crossed`);
      }
      if (k > 0) { allocated += k * CFG.estTrialUsd; planned.push({ ...r, k }); }
    }
    if (!planned.length) continue;
    const outs = await parallel(planned.map(r => () => runCell(r, tag)));
    for (const o of outs) if (o) results.push(...o);
    log(`${tag}: ${Math.min(i + CFG.batch, requests.length)}/${requests.length} cells done. Trial spend $${r2(ledger.spentUsd)}.`);
  }
  return results;
}

async function audit(trials, tag) {
  const ids = trials.filter(t => t.status === 'completed').map(t => t.trial_id);
  if (!ids.length) return true;
  const res = await call(`You audit eval trials for peeks at the answer key. You do not grade anything.
For each trial id below, open ${RUN_DIR}/traces/<trial_id>.json. It records every tool call the triage agent made, with arguments and results.
Flag a trial if any tool call, argument, or result mentions any of these strings: ${FORBIDDEN.join(', ')}.
Give the exact line or field as evidence.
List every trial id whose trace file is missing.
Do not edit or delete any file.

Trial ids:
${ids.join('\n')}`, { label: `peek scan (${tag})`, phase: tag === 'base' ? 'Trials' : 'Top-up', schema: AUDIT_SCHEMA, model: CFG.harnessModel });
  if (!res) { halt(`peek scan did not run for ${tag} trials`); return false; }
  const byId = new Map(trials.map(t => [t.trial_id, t]));
  for (const f of res.flagged) { const t = byId.get(f.trial_id); if (t) { t.voided = true; t.void_reason = `peek: ${f.evidence}`; } }
  for (const id of res.traces_missing) { const t = byId.get(id); if (t) { t.voided = true; t.void_reason = 'no trace, so the peek scan cannot clear it'; } }
  const done = all.filter(t => t.status === 'completed');
  const voided = done.filter(t => t.voided);
  for (const t of voided) if (!ledger.voids.some(v => v.trial_id === t.trial_id)) ledger.voids.push({ trial_id: t.trial_id, reason: t.void_reason });
  log(`peek scan (${tag}): ${res.traces_scanned} traces scanned, ${res.flagged.length} flagged, ${res.traces_missing.length} missing.`);
  if (done.length && voided.length / done.length > CFG.maxVoidFrac) {
    halt(`${voided.length} of ${done.length} completed trials were voided, above the limit of ${CFG.maxVoidFrac}. Possible leaked answer key.`);
    return false;
  }
  return true;
}

async function grade(trials, tag) {
  const rows = trials.filter(t => t.status === 'completed' && !t.voided);
  if (!rows.length) return true;
  const payload = rows.map(t => JSON.stringify({ trial_id: t.trial_id, ticket_id: t.ticket, label: t.label ?? null })).join('\n');
  const res = await call(`You run the code grader. You do not judge anything yourself.
1. Write the lines between the markers to ${RUN_DIR}/labels-${tag}.jsonl exactly as given.
2. Run: ${CFG.gradeCmd} --answers ${CFG.answersFile} --in ${RUN_DIR}/labels-${tag}.jsonl --out ${RUN_DIR}/grades-${tag}.jsonl
3. Read ${RUN_DIR}/grades-${tag}.jsonl and return every row as written. Do not change any value. Report the exit code.

<<<LABELS
${payload}
LABELS>>>`, { label: `grade (${tag})`, phase: tag === 'base' ? 'Grade' : 'Top-up', schema: GRADE_SCHEMA, model: CFG.harnessModel });
  if (!res) { halt(`grader agent failed on ${tag} trials`); return false; }
  if (res.exit_code !== 0) { halt(`grade.py exited with ${res.exit_code} on ${tag} trials. Broken grader.`); return false; }
  const byId = new Map(res.rows.map(r => [r.trial_id, r]));
  const missing = rows.filter(t => !byId.has(t.trial_id));
  if (missing.length || res.rows.length !== rows.length) {
    halt(`grade.py returned ${res.rows.length} rows for ${rows.length} trials. Missing: ${missing.slice(0, 5).map(t => t.trial_id).join(', ')}. Broken grader.`);
    return false;
  }
  for (const t of rows) {
    const g = byId.get(t.trial_id);
    t.category_ok = g.category_ok;
    t.priority_ok = g.priority_ok;
    t.both_ok = g.category_ok && g.priority_ok;
  }
  log(`grade (${tag}): ${rows.length} trials graded.`);
  return true;
}

async function judgeTicket([ticket, ts]) {
  if (ledger.spentUsd + ledger.judgeUsd + CFG.estJudgeUsd > CFG.capUsd) {
    ledger.capHit = true;
    ledger.skips.push({ what: `judge ${ticket}`, why: `spend cap $${CFG.capUsd}` });
    log(`skip judge for ${ticket}: the spend cap would be crossed`);
    for (const t of ts) t.tone_missing = true;
    return;
  }
  ledger.judgeUsd += CFG.estJudgeUsd;
  const order = shuffle(ts, `${RR}:${ticket}`);
  const byRid = new Map(order.map((t, i) => [`R${i + 1}`, t]));
  const blocks = order.map((t, i) => `<reply id="R${i + 1}">\n${t.reply}\n</reply>`).join('\n');
  const res = await call(`You are the tone judge. Read ${CFG.judgeFile} and apply it exactly.
Read the ticket at ${RUN_DIR}/tickets/${ticket}.json.
Below are draft first replies to that ticket. Different setups wrote them, and they appear in random order. You are not told which setup wrote which reply.
Judge tone only, as ${CFG.judgeFile} defines it. Do not judge the category or the priority.
Return one score for every reply id.

${blocks}`, { label: `judge ${ticket}`, phase: 'Judge', schema: JUDGE_SCHEMA, model: CFG.judgeModel });
  if (res) for (const s of res.scores) { const t = byRid.get(s.rid); if (t) { t.tone = s.tone; t.tone_pass = s.pass; t.tone_reason = s.reason; } }
  for (const t of ts) if (typeof t.tone_pass !== 'boolean') t.tone_missing = true;
}

function metricsFor(config) {
  const ts = all.filter(t => t.config === config);
  const done = ts.filter(t => t.status === 'completed' && !t.voided);
  const byCell = groupBy(done, 'cell');
  const baseByCell = new Map([...byCell].map(([k, v]) => [k, v.slice().sort((a, b) => a.n - b.n).slice(0, CFG.trials)]));
  const cellRate = (pick, m) => mean([...m.values()].map(c => rate(c.map(pick))));
  const block = m => ({
    category_acc: cellRate(t => t.category_ok, m),
    priority_acc: cellRate(t => t.priority_ok, m),
    both_acc: cellRate(t => t.both_ok, m),
    tone_pass: cellRate(t => t.tone_pass, m),
  });
  return {
    note: CONFIG_NOTES[config] || 'see runner config',
    cell_weighted_all_trials: block(byCell),
    base_trials_only: block(baseByCell),
    tone_mean: mean(done.map(t => t.tone)),
    runtime_s_mean: mean(done.map(t => t.runtime_s)),
    tool_calls_mean: mean(done.map(t => t.tool_calls)),
    tool_errors_mean: mean(done.map(t => t.tool_errors)),
    trials_with_tool_error: rate(done.map(t => isNum(t.tool_errors) ? t.tool_errors > 0 : null)),
    tokens_mean: mean(done.map(t => (isNum(t.input_tokens) && isNum(t.output_tokens)) ? t.input_tokens + t.output_tokens : null)),
    cost_usd_total: r2(sum(ts.map(t => t.cost_usd))),
    trials_completed: done.length,
    trials_not_completed: ts.filter(t => t.status !== 'completed').length,
    trials_voided: ts.filter(t => t.voided).length,
    tone_missing: done.filter(t => t.tone_missing).length,
    cells_total: cells.filter(c => c.config === config).length,
    cells_with_full_trials: [...byCell.values()].filter(c => c.length >= CFG.trials).length,
  };
}

function finish() {
  return {
    round: ROUND,
    run_dir: RUN_DIR,
    status: ledger.halted ? 'halted' : ledger.capHit ? 'capped' : 'complete',
    halt_reason: ledger.halted,
    args_used: CFG,
    metrics: out.metrics,
    ceilings: out.ceilings,
    failure_analysis: out.failures,
    critic: out.critic,
    spend: { trials_usd: r2(ledger.spentUsd), judge_usd_estimated: r2(ledger.judgeUsd), judge_reserve_usd: r2(judgeReserve), cap_usd: CFG.capUsd },
    agents_used: ledger.agents,
    harness_errors: ledger.harnessErrors,
    skips: ledger.skips,
    voids: ledger.voids,
    trials: all,
  };
}

// ---------- main ----------
async function main() {
  log(`Round ${ROUND}. Configs: ${CFG.configs.map(c => `${c} (${CONFIG_NOTES[c] || 'see runner config'})`).join('; ')}. Cap $${CFG.capUsd}. Run dir ${RUN_DIR}.`);
  log('Judge note: the tone judge is Claude Opus and the trials run Claude Sonnet. No judge from another model family is available, so tone scores may share blind spots with the agent.');

  phase('Setup');
  const setup = await call(`You prepare inputs for an eval of the triage agent.
1. Read ${CFG.ticketsFile}. Each line is one ticket.
2. For each ticket write ${RUN_DIR}/tickets/<ticket_id>.json with only the fields the triage agent sees as input: ticket_id, subject, body, and customer metadata. Drop category, priority, label, and any reference reply.
3. Read back every file you wrote. List any file that still has a key named category, priority, label, or reference_reply.
4. Return the ticket ids in file order.
Write nothing outside ${RUN_DIR}/tickets/.`, { label: 'setup', phase: 'Setup', schema: SETUP_SCHEMA, model: CFG.harnessModel });
  if (!setup) { halt('setup agent failed'); return finish(); }
  if (setup.label_keys_found.length) { halt(`leaked answer key: label fields remain in ${setup.label_keys_found.join(', ')}`); return finish(); }
  if (setup.ticket_ids.length !== CFG.ticketsExpected) { halt(`expected ${CFG.ticketsExpected} tickets, found ${setup.ticket_ids.length}`); return finish(); }

  for (const config of CFG.configs) for (const ticket of setup.ticket_ids) cells.push({ cell: `${config}:${ticket}`, config, ticket });
  if (CFG.only) cells = cells.filter(c => CFG.only.includes(c.cell));
  if (!cells.length) { halt('args.only matched no cells'); return finish(); }
  const ticketsInScope = [...new Set(cells.map(c => c.ticket))];
  judgeReserve = ticketsInScope.length * CFG.estJudgeUsd;
  if (judgeReserve >= CFG.capUsd) { halt(`judge reserve $${r2(judgeReserve)} leaves no trial budget under the $${CFG.capUsd} cap`); return finish(); }
  log(`${cells.length} cells x ${CFG.trials} trials. Judge reserve $${r2(judgeReserve)}. Trial budget $${r2(CFG.capUsd - judgeReserve)}.`);

  phase('Trials');
  const base = await runCells(cells.map(c => ({ ...c, want: CFG.trials, start: 1 })), 'base');
  all.push(...base);
  if (!(await audit(base, 'base'))) return finish();

  phase('Grade');
  if (!(await grade(base, 'base'))) return finish();

  phase('Top-up');
  const requests = [];
  let splitCells = 0;
  let refillCells = 0;
  for (const c of cells) {
    const done = all.filter(t => t.cell === c.cell && t.status === 'completed' && !t.voided);
    const refill = Math.max(0, CFG.trials - done.length);
    const passes = done.filter(t => t.both_ok).length;
    const split = passes > 0 && passes < done.length;
    let want = refill;
    if (refill) refillCells += 1;
    if (split && splitCells < CFG.topUpCellsMax) { want += CFG.topUpPerCell; splitCells += 1; }
    else if (split) log(`split cell ${c.cell} gets no top-up: the cap of ${CFG.topUpCellsMax} split cells is reached`);
    if (want) requests.push({ ...c, want, start: nextIndex[c.cell] || 1 });
  }
  log(`Top-up: ${splitCells} split cells get ${CFG.topUpPerCell} extra trials. ${refillCells} cells get refills for harness errors, voids, or skips.`);
  if (requests.length) {
    const extra = await runCells(requests, 'topup');
    all.push(...extra);
    if (!(await audit(extra, 'topup'))) return finish();
    if (!(await grade(extra, 'topup'))) return finish();
  }

  phase('Judge');
  const judgeable = all.filter(t => t.status === 'completed' && !t.voided && typeof t.reply === 'string' && t.reply.length);
  await inBatches([...groupBy(judgeable, 'ticket').entries()], judgeTicket);

  phase('Synthesis');
  out.metrics = Object.fromEntries(CFG.configs.map(c => [c, metricsFor(c)]));
  out.ceilings = ['category_acc', 'priority_acc', 'both_acc', 'tone_pass'].filter(k => CFG.configs.every(c => out.metrics[c].cell_weighted_all_trials[k] === 1));
  if (out.ceilings.length) log(`Ceiling: every config scored 1.0 on ${out.ceilings.join(', ')}. Record those predictions as not scorable and check once for a leak or a grader bug.`);

  const failed = all.filter(t => t.status === 'completed' && !t.voided && (t.both_ok === false || t.tone_pass === false || (isNum(t.tool_errors) && t.tool_errors > 0)));
  const failLines = failed.slice(0, 200).map(t => JSON.stringify({
    trial_id: t.trial_id, config: t.config, ticket: t.ticket, label: t.label,
    category_ok: t.category_ok, priority_ok: t.priority_ok, tone: t.tone, tone_reason: t.tone_reason, tool_errors: t.tool_errors,
  })).join('\n');
  out.failures = failed.length ? await call(`You analyze failures from an eval of the triage agent. Configs: ${CFG.configs.map(c => `${c} = ${CONFIG_NOTES[c]}`).join('; ')}.
You may read ${CFG.answersFile}, ${CFG.judgeFile}, ${RUN_DIR}/tickets/, ${RUN_DIR}/traces/, and spe/failures.md.
Group the failed trials below into failure types. For each type give a short name, the kind (label, priority, tone, tool, harness), what happens, how to spot it, the trial ids it was seen in, the configs, the count, and a fix.
If a type matches an F-number already in spe/failures.md, give that F-number. Otherwise leave existing_f_id null.
Flag any case where the reference answer itself looks wrong. That is a grader failure, not an agent failure.
${failed.length > 200 ? `Only the first 200 of ${failed.length} failed trials are listed.\n` : ''}
${failLines}`, { label: 'failure analysis', phase: 'Synthesis', schema: FAIL_SCHEMA, model: CFG.harnessModel }) : { types: [] };

  const summary = JSON.stringify({ metrics: out.metrics, ceilings: out.ceilings, skips: ledger.skips, voids: ledger.voids.length, harness_errors: ledger.harnessErrors, spend: { trials_usd: r2(ledger.spentUsd), judge_usd_estimated: r2(ledger.judgeUsd), cap_usd: CFG.capUsd }, cells: cells.length, trials_per_cell: CFG.trials, dry_run: !!CFG.only });
  out.critic = await call(`You check whether an eval run is complete. You do not edit any file.
Read spe/predictions/${RR}.yaml and spe/plans/${RR}.md.
Check the run summary below against them:
1. Does every predicted metric have a measured value for every config? List each one that does not.
2. Does every cell have at least ${CFG.trials} completed, unvoided trials? Name the gaps.
3. Do the skips, voids, harness errors, missing tone scores, or spend change what the numbers can support?
4. Does any part of the approved plan's harness steps not appear in the run?
Do not score the predictions. That happens at close-out.

${summary}`, { label: 'completeness critic', phase: 'Synthesis', schema: CRITIC_SCHEMA, model: CFG.harnessModel });

  log(`Done. Trial spend $${r2(ledger.spentUsd)}, judge spend (estimated) $${r2(ledger.judgeUsd)}, cap $${CFG.capUsd}. ${ledger.skips.length} skips, ${ledger.voids.length} voids, ${ledger.agents} agents.`);
  return finish();
}

return await main();
